  "worked_solution": "The Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model is given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032}=ax-bxy \\\\ {y}^{\u2032}=-cy+dxy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,d$ are positive real constants. \n\nFirst, recall that a derivative represents a $\\text{rate of change}.$\n\nFor the ${y}^{\u2032}$ equation, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=4y-0.5xy.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y$ must represent the $\\text{prey}.$ Indeed,\n\n- it grows exponentially in the absence of predators (the $4y$ term), and\n\n- decreases when interacting with predators (the $-0.5xy$ term).",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
